21708      data Children;
21709      input ID City$ @@;
21710      do i=1 to 4;
21711      input Age Smoke Symptom @@;
21712      output;
21713      end;
21714      datalines;

NOTE: SAS went to a new line when INPUT statement reached past the end of a line.
NOTE: The data set WORK.CHILDREN has 100 observations and 6 variables.

21740      ;
21741      proc gee data=Children descending;
21742      class ID City;
21743      model Symptom = City Age Smoke / dist=bin link=logit;
21744      repeated subject=ID / type=exch covb corrw;
21745      run;

NOTE: PROC GEE is modeling the probability that Symptom='1'.
